cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the accompanying article."
type: software
title: "DMG_HE_IF: prediction of spatial protein markers from H&E for \"Mapping the Tumor Microenvironment of Pediatric Diffuse Midline Glioma using a Spatial Proteomic Atlas with AI-Based Application\""
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ams-unibe-ch/DMG_HE_IF"
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX   # add the Zenodo concept DOI after the first release
abstract: "Code accompanying the article \"Mapping the Tumor Microenvironment of Pediatric Diffuse Midline Glioma using a Spatial Proteomic Atlas with AI-Based Application\". The pipeline predicts the presence of marker-positive cells for 22 multiplexed immunofluorescence markers in 100 µm tiles of virtual H&E images of a pediatric brain tumor tissue microarray, using pathology foundation-model embeddings (UNI, Virchow, Prov-GigaPath, CTransPath, RetCCL, REMEDIS) and lightGBM classifiers."
keywords:
  - "diffuse midline glioma"
  - "DIPG"
  - "digital pathology"
  - "foundation models"
  - "multiplexed immunofluorescence"
  - "H&E"
  - "tissue microarray"
  - "tumor microenvironment"
  - "machine learning"
